engsyn: word-level enye phonetic preprocessor (user)

User-supplied eci_engsyn.c: in-word enye units (UTF-8 or Western)
become ny/Ny, word-initial before a becomes nyah/Nyah, standalone
stays as-is for the screen reader echo. Wired into both text entry
doors with the same lifetime handling. Upstream comments stripped in
passing.
Applied at build time so CI builds the same tree.
